## Experiment 2: Study guide

### Prompt

Create a concise study guide from the uploaded sources. Organise it into key concepts, practical tasks, evidence required and common risks. Use only the uploaded sources.
### Result

Here is a study guide synthesized directly from your assessment overview and rubric documents:
1. Key Concepts
Cloud Service & Deployment Models: Classifying enterprise environments into SaaS, PaaS, or IaaS, mapping deployment structures, and defining security boundaries via the Shared Responsibility Model
.
Conversational AI Architecture: Designing intent-driven conversational flows in Dialogflow (utilising intents, entities, parameters, decision pathways, fallback logic, and escalation triggers) and linking chatbots conceptually to enterprise cloud processes
.
LLM Message Triage & Prompt Design: Structuring prompts to extract standardized JSON payloads (issue category, urgency, sentiment, follow-up flags, and team allocation) and evaluating model performance against rule-based or zero-shot baselines
.
AI Productivity & Academic Evaluation: Evaluating cloud-based note-taking platforms like NotebookLM across academic and policy workflows, balancing capability against accuracy, hallucination risks, and over-reliance
.
Responsible AI & Cloud Governance: Integrating ethics, user consent, data minimisation, privacy controls, accessibility, human oversight, and regulatory compliance into cloud-enabled ESG platforms
.
2. Practical Tasks
Task 1 (Q1, 17 Marks) — Dialogflow ESG Chatbot: Select a targeted ESG use case (e.g. incident reporting or energy guidance), describe five chatbot functionalities, address ethics/governance/accessibility, prototype a Dialogflow flow with 3–5 intents and routing logic, and record a <2 minute executive video
.
Task 2 (Q2, 8 Marks) — Cloud Security Audit: Investigate a real-world cloud or hybrid security breach from the past five years, detail compromised data/systems, map the SaaS/PaaS/IaaS architecture and shared responsibility split, and recommend 3–5 preventative cloud platform controls
.
Task 3 (Q3, 7 Marks) — LLM Operational Message Triage: Refine a JSON prompt template, test operational ESG messages on an LLM, benchmark classification performance against a Hugging Face or rule-based baseline, evaluate operational risks, and design an Azure cloud deployment architecture
.
Task 4 (Q4, 8 Marks) — NotebookLM Feasibility Study: Demonstrate key academic/ESG workflows in Google's NotebookLM, critically analyze output accuracy and operational limitations, and log experimental results in a GitHub repository
.
3. Evidence Required
Written Report: A report formatted with APA 7 citations and clear section headings for Q1, Q2, Q3, and Q4, supported by architecture diagrams, screenshots, and tables
.
Executive Demonstration Video: A short demonstration video (under 2 minutes) introducing the chatbot and workflow rationale, hosted on Microsoft Stream or Echo365 with marker access enabled
.
Dialogflow Implementation Screenshots: Clear screenshots showing conversation flows, pages, intents, entities, routing rules, and sample transcripts
.
GitHub Repository: A link to an accessible GitHub repository containing experiment logs, prompt test outputs, and evidence for Q3 and Q4
.
AI Acknowledgement Form: A completed AI acknowledgement form declaring permissible generative AI usage under the AI Exploration category
.
4. Common Risks
Generative AI & LLM Risks: Unverified AI outputs, hallucinations, algorithmic bias, data privacy breaches, lack of human oversight, and misrouting sensitive operational escalations
.
Conversational Design Failures: Broken user journeys, missing fallback responses, uncaptured entity parameters, and failure to integrate inclusive or accessible design features
.
Cloud Security & Configuration Gaps: Infrastructure misconfigurations, improper identity and access management (IAM), missing audit logs, and misunderstandings of shared responsibility boundaries
.
Logistical & Submission Risks: Submitting broken links for the video or GitHub repo, exceeding the 2-minute video cutoff, missing required AI acknowledgement forms, or omitting prompt JSON fields
.
